Implement user story MOCK3-1: Riders aged exactly 65 are charged the adult fare

## Story Description
The fare rules say riders aged 65 and over pay the concession fare. A rider aged exactly 65 is charged the full adult fare of 350 cents instead of 175. Riders aged 66 and above are charged correctly, so the boundary itself is wrong rather than the rule.

## Acceptance Criteria
- A rider aged exactly 65 with no pass is charged the concession fare.
- A rider aged 64 with no pass is still charged the base fare.
- The existing fare behaviour for children, pass holders and adults is unchanged.

